            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to chime, then the Gujarati for to be itching to dance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: રાસ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાસ — rās — \"raas (a stick dance)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો આજે રાત્રે વરસાદ નહીં પડે તો આપણે રાસ રમીશું. jo āje rātre varsād nahī̃ paḍe to āpaṇe rās ramīśũ. If it doesn't rain tonight, we'll dance raas."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાસ (rās) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit rāsa, a country dance of cowherds (Monier-Williams). Gujarati \"plays\" it: રાસ રમવો."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
